# R8 rules for the release build. The libraries bring their own rules, so this file
# only holds what is DuckCount's to say.

# The source is public, so renamed classes would hide nothing, and a stack trace from a
# user's phone, or a class name in an error message, reads as is with no mapping file.
-dontobfuscate
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable

# The Rust library's bindings, generated by uniffi, call it through JNA, which finds by
# reflection the native functions they register, the fields of the structures they pass
# and the method of each callback the library calls back, and whose own native code calls
# into its Java classes by name. None of it would survive R8 otherwise.
-keep class com.sun.jna.** { *; }
-keep class * extends com.sun.jna.** { *; }
-keep class uniffi.** { *; }
-dontwarn java.awt.**
